# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository, whatever platform it was
# committed from. Four CSV here were once committed with CRLF against an
# LF-only declaration, which made a fresh clone report 871 modified lines
# before anyone had run anything. The catch-all covers file types nobody has
# added yet.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.csv   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf

# Never diffed, never munged, should any land here.
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.npz   binary

# No linguist-generated / linguist-vendored marks in this repository, unlike
# Multiaxis_ECI. The feeds under 0_input/feed/ are upstream snapshots and
# 2_database/ is regenerated output, so both look like obvious candidates. But
# marking them collapses them in GitHub's diff view, and reading that diff is
# how a refresh is reviewed here (the monthly refresh opens a pull request).
# Hiding it would remove the review step this repository is built around.
